---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About the Stockholm Centre for the Ethics of War and Peace: our mission, history, and funding."
>
  <PageHero
    title="About the Centre"
    subtitle="Rigorous philosophy on the morality of armed conflict"
    breadcrumb={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "About" }]}
  />

  <div class="container-page py-16">
    <div class="prose-academic">
      <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-text">
        The Stockholm Centre for the Ethics of War and Peace is an
        interdisciplinary research centre based in the Department of Philosophy
        at Stockholm University. We are dedicated to the rigorous philosophical
        study of the moral, political, and legal questions raised by war, armed
        conflict, and the pursuit of peace.
      </p>

      <h2>Our mission</h2>
      <p>
        War confronts us with some of the hardest questions in ethics. When, if
        ever, is it permissible to kill? Who may be targeted, and who must be
        protected? What do victors owe to the vanquished, and what does a just
        peace require? The Centre exists to address these questions with the
        analytical rigour of contemporary moral and political philosophy, while
        remaining engaged with the realities of conflict and the work of those
        who study it across law, political science, and history.
      </p>

      <h2>History</h2>
      <p>
        Founded in 2012, the Centre has grown into one of the leading
        international hubs for research on the ethics of war. It hosts
        postdoctoral researchers and doctoral candidates, convenes regular
        workshops and reading groups, and runs its flagship
        <em>Conversations on War</em> series, which brings leading thinkers into
        public dialogue. The Centre is also known for its journal symposia —
        collections of critical essays organised around an important book or
        topic and published in leading philosophy journals.
      </p>

      <h2>Funding</h2>
      <p>
        The Centre's research has been supported by a range of funders,
        including the Knut and Alice Wallenberg Foundation through the Wallenberg
        Academy Fellows programme, Riksbankens Jubileumsfond, and Stockholm
        University. This support enables us to sustain a vibrant community of
        researchers and an active programme of events and public engagement.
      </p>

      <h2>Join us</h2>
      <p>
        We welcome enquiries from prospective doctoral students, visiting
        researchers, and collaborators. If you would like to learn more about
        the Centre or explore working with us, please get in touch.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 rounded-lg border border-border bg-white p-8 text-center">
      <h3 class="text-2xl">Get in touch</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted">
        Questions about our research, events, or collaboration?
      </p>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-ghost mt-5">Contact the Centre</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
